---
import Base from "~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "~/components/PageHero.astro";
import {site} from "~/site.config";

const title = "Device Policy";
const subtitle = "";
const description = "";

// Breadcrumbs: last item is current page (no href)
const breadcrumb = [
  {label: "Home", href: "/"},
  {label: "About"},
  {label: title},
];
---

<Base title={`${title} | ${site.name}`} description={description}>
  <PageHero title={title} subtitle={subtitle} breadcrumb={breadcrumb} />

  <!-- Long-form content gets Typography styles -->

  <article
    class="prose prose-slate md:prose-lg mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10
           prose-a:text-bulldog-orange prose-a:no-underline hover:prose-a:underline
           prose-img:rounded-xl prose-headings:font-semibold"
  >
    <h2>Personal Electronic Device Policy c. 2026</h2>
    <p>
      As we prepare for the upcoming school year, we want to remind families
      about our Personal Electronic Device (PED) policy.
    </p>
    <p>
      All personal electronic devices - including cell phones, smartwatches,
      wireless earbuds, and similar devices - must be turned off and securely
      stored in students' assigned lockers from 7:00 a/m/ through 2:20 p.m.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every student will be assigned a locker. Students who bring a personal
      electronic device to school must turn the device off before the start of
      the school day, secure the device in their assigned locker, and keep the
      device stored in the locker throughout the school day.
    </p>
    <p>
      We appreciate the support of our families as we work together to create a
      focused, respectful, and distraction-free learning environment for all
      students.
    </p>
    <p>
      For further information regarding the implementation of Maine's
      bell-to-bell personal electronic device policy, please visit the following
      website:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a
          href="https://mainedoenews.net/2026/05/20/priority-notice-implementation-of-maines-bell-to-bell-personal-electronic-device-policy/"
          >Maine DOE News</a
        >
      </li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</Base>
